          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For dry block, inside or out, the most reliable system is one coat of a high-solids block filler such as Sherwin-Williams Loxon Block Surfacer followed by two coats of a 100 percent acrylic masonry paint such as Behr Premium Masonry, Stucco and Brick. For damp basement block, skip that system and brush on two coats of DRYLOK Extreme after fixing outdoor drainage.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, the wall decides the result before the paint does. Let new block cure, remove efflorescence, test for moisture with a sheet of plastic, and fill the pores. Do those four things and even mid-priced paint will hold for years.
